    {
      "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-1-sec-372-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "372 5  Alternative verdict",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-1-sec-372-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if, in a prosecution for an offence against\nsection 372.1, the trier of fact is not satisfied that the defendant is\nguilty of the offence, but is satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that\nthe defendant is guilty of an offence against section 372.2.\n\n(2) The trier of fact may find the defendant not guilty of the offence\nagainst section 372.1 but guilty of the offence against\nsection 372.2, so long as the defendant has been accorded\nprocedural fairness in relation to that finding of guilt.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if, in a prosecution for an offence against\nsection 372.1, the trier of fact is not satisfied that the defendant is\nguilty of the offence, but is satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that\nthe defendant is guilty of an offence against section 372.2.\n\n(2) The trier of fact may find the defendant not guilty of the offence\nagainst section 372.1 but guilty of the offence against\nsection 372.2, so long as the defendant has been accorded\nprocedural fairness in relation to that finding of guilt.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-1-sec-372-5-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-1-sec-372-5-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9d1de086670b215323e6bc9c1ea0963eeed0ed41249fbbc778128fb3d9ef7bd5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-1-sec-372-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "372 5  Alternative verdict",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if, in a prosecution for an offence against\nsection 372.1, the trier of fact is not satisfied that the defendant is\nguilty of the offence, but is satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that\nthe defendant is guilty of an offence against section 372.2.\n\n(2) The trier of fact may find the defendant not guilty of the offence\nagainst section 372.1 but guilty of the offence against\nsection 372.2, so long as the defendant has been accorded\nprocedural fairness in relation to that finding of guilt."
    },
