    {
      "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-1-sec-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 Law and Justice Legislation Amendment (Identity Crimes and Other Measures) Act 2011",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-1-sec-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "No. 3, 2011\n\n(b) subject to subsection (2)—any proceedings (whether civil or\ncriminal) have been or can be taken against a person for or in\nrelation to the dealing, or are pending.\n\n(2) The magistrate must not issue a certificate under section 375.1 if\ndoing so would prejudice any proceedings.\n\n(3) The certificate is not admissible in any proceedings.",
      "skos:definition": "No. 3, 2011\n\n(b) subject to subsection (2)—any proceedings (whether civil or\ncriminal) have been or can be taken against a person for or in\nrelation to the dealing, or are pending.\n\n(2) The magistrate must not issue a certificate under section 375.1 if\ndoing so would prejudice any proceedings.\n\n(3) The certificate is not admissible in any proceedings.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-1-sec-8-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-1-sec-8-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3a6c84e21520f88f8911ffa56a2d36b7f48b7b30898970a20569023425a84897"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-1-sec-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 Law and Justice Legislation Amendment (Identity Crimes and Other Measures) Act 2011",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "No. 3, 2011\n\n(b) subject to subsection (2)—any proceedings (whether civil or\ncriminal) have been or can be taken against a person for or in\nrelation to the dealing, or are pending.\n\n(2) The magistrate must not issue a certificate under section 375.1 if\ndoing so would prejudice any proceedings.\n\n(3) The certificate is not admissible in any proceedings."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-1-sec-8-ss-2",
