    {
      "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-31",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31 Judicial proceeding and tribunal definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-2-sec-31"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "In this Act:\nfederal judicial proceeding means:\n\n(a) a judicial proceeding in or before:\n\n(i) a federal court; or\n\n(ii) a court exercising federal jurisdiction; or\n\n(iii) a court of a Territory; or\n\n(b) a judicial proceeding before a body or person acting under a\nlaw of:\n\n(i) the Commonwealth; or\n\n(ii) a Territory.\njudicial proceeding means (other than in section 3L):\n\n(a) a proceeding in or before a court; or\n\n(b) a proceeding:\n\n(i) before a body, or a person, acting under a law of the\nCommonwealth, of a State or of a Territory; and\n\n(ii) in which evidence may be taken on oath.\njudicial tribunal means a body or person (other than a court)\nbefore whom a judicial proceeding is conducted.",
      "skos:definition": "In this Act:\nfederal judicial proceeding means:\n\n(a) a judicial proceeding in or before:\n\n(i) a federal court; or\n\n(ii) a court exercising federal jurisdiction; or\n\n(iii) a court of a Territory; or\n\n(b) a judicial proceeding before a body or person acting under a\nlaw of:\n\n(i) the Commonwealth; or\n\n(ii) a Territory.\njudicial proceeding means (other than in section 3L):\n\n(a) a proceeding in or before a court; or\n\n(b) a proceeding:\n\n(i) before a body, or a person, acting under a law of the\nCommonwealth, of a State or of a Territory; and\n\n(ii) in which evidence may be taken on oath.\njudicial tribunal means a body or person (other than a court)\nbefore whom a judicial proceeding is conducted.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-31-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-31-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-31-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a34cb700dceb36a8278f87173588992dfdfb15df325d022fa685c89feeba02a2",
      "skos:note": "Defines federal judicial proceeding and judicial tribunal."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-2-sec-31",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31 Judicial proceeding and tribunal definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "In this Act:\nfederal judicial proceeding means:\n\n(a) a judicial proceeding in or before:\n\n(i) a federal court; or\n\n(ii) a court exercising federal jurisdiction; or\n\n(iii) a court of a Territory; or\n\n(b) a judicial proceeding before a body or person acting under a\nlaw of:\n\n(i) the Commonwealth; or\n\n(ii) a Territory.\njudicial proceeding means (other than in section 3L):\n\n(a) a proceeding in or before a court; or\n\n(b) a proceeding:\n\n(i) before a body, or a person, acting under a law of the\nCommonwealth, of a State or of a Territory; and\n\n(ii) in which evidence may be taken on oath.\njudicial tribunal means a body or person (other than a court)\nbefore whom a judicial proceeding is conducted."
    },
