    {
      "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-35",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35 Giving false testimony",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-2-sec-35"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person gives false testimony touching a matter; and\n\n(b) the person does so:\n\n(i) in a judicial proceeding; or\n\n(ii) with the intention of instituting a judicial proceeding;\nand\n\n(c) the matter is material in the judicial proceeding; and\n\n(d) the judicial proceeding is a federal judicial proceeding.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(2) Strict liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n\n(3) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(d) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, it is immaterial:\n\n(a) whether the testimony is given:\n\n(i) on oath or not on oath; or\n\n(ii) orally or in writing; or\n\n(b) whether the court or judicial tribunal to which the testimony\nis given:\n\n(i) is properly constituted; or\n\n(ii) is held in the proper place; or\n\n(c) whether the person who gave the testimony is a competent\nwitness; or\n\n(d) whether the testimony is admissible.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person gives false testimony touching a matter; and\n\n(b) the person does so:\n\n(i) in a judicial proceeding; or\n\n(ii) with the intention of instituting a judicial proceeding;\nand\n\n(c) the matter is material in the judicial proceeding; and\n\n(d) the judicial proceeding is a federal judicial proceeding.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(2) Strict liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n\n(3) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(d) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, it is immaterial:\n\n(a) whether the testimony is given:\n\n(i) on oath or not on oath; or\n\n(ii) orally or in writing; or\n\n(b) whether the court or judicial tribunal to which the testimony\nis given:\n\n(i) is properly constituted; or\n\n(ii) is held in the proper place; or\n\n(c) whether the person who gave the testimony is a competent\nwitness; or\n\n(d) whether the testimony is admissible.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-35-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-35-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-35-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-35-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8732e8517eab6bd4fcc6b4987976095e6f6e9ecf68b728d4b7a02375cac9c095"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-2-sec-35",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35 Giving false testimony",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person gives false testimony touching a matter; and\n\n(b) the person does so:\n\n(i) in a judicial proceeding; or\n\n(ii) with the intention of instituting a judicial proceeding;\nand\n\n(c) the matter is material in the judicial proceeding; and\n\n(d) the judicial proceeding is a federal judicial proceeding.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(2) Strict liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n\n(3) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(d) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, it is immaterial:\n\n(a) whether the testimony is given:\n\n(i) on oath or not on oath; or\n\n(ii) orally or in writing; or\n\n(b) whether the court or judicial tribunal to which the testimony\nis given:\n\n(i) is properly constituted; or\n\n(ii) is held in the proper place; or\n\n(c) whether the person who gave the testimony is a competent\nwitness; or\n\n(d) whether the testimony is admissible."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-35-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35(1) Giving false testimony",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
