    {
      "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-35-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35(4) Giving false testimony",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-2-sec-35-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "(4) For the purposes of this section, it is immaterial:\n\n(a) whether the testimony is given:\n\n(i) on oath or not on oath; or\n\n(ii) orally or in writing; or\n\n(b) whether the court or judicial tribunal to which the testimony\nis given:\n\n(i) is properly constituted; or\n\n(ii) is held in the proper place; or\n\n(c) whether the person who gave the testimony is a competent\nwitness; or\n\n(d) whether the testimony is admissible.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) For the purposes of this section, it is immaterial:\n\n(a) whether the testimony is given:\n\n(i) on oath or not on oath; or\n\n(ii) orally or in writing; or\n\n(b) whether the court or judicial tribunal to which the testimony\nis given:\n\n(i) is properly constituted; or\n\n(ii) is held in the proper place; or\n\n(c) whether the person who gave the testimony is a competent\nwitness; or\n\n(d) whether the testimony is admissible.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-35"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-35-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-35-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a8c831671051c07fc7c17a90839554d6e344d4f98b230e9ee2fe4f3b2af405ba",
      "skos:note": "Giving false testimony is not a requirement for the purposes of this section."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-2-sec-35-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35(4) Giving false testimony",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "(4) For the purposes of this section, it is immaterial:\n\n(a) whether the testimony is given:\n\n(i) on oath or not on oath; or\n\n(ii) orally or in writing; or\n\n(b) whether the court or judicial tribunal to which the testimony\nis given:\n\n(i) is properly constituted; or\n\n(ii) is held in the proper place; or\n\n(c) whether the person who gave the testimony is a competent\nwitness; or\n\n(d) whether the testimony is admissible."
    },
    {
