      },
      "cml:premiseText": "This section does not require testimony.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Testimony is exempted."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-36",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "36 Fabricating evidence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-2-sec-36"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) fabricates evidence; or\n\n(ii) makes use of fabricated evidence; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003\n\nAdministration of justice offences  Schedule 2\nAmendment of the Crimes Act 1914  Part 1\n\nLaw and Justice Legislation Amendment (Identity Crimes and Other Measures) Act 2011       No.\n3, 2011            15\n\n(b) the person does so with the intention of misleading a court or\njudicial tribunal in a judicial proceeding; and\n\n(c) the judicial proceeding is a federal judicial proceeding.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) fabricates evidence; or\n\n(ii) makes use of fabricated evidence; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003\n\nAdministration of justice offences  Schedule 2\nAmendment of the Crimes Act 1914  Part 1\n\nLaw and Justice Legislation Amendment (Identity Crimes and Other Measures) Act 2011       No.\n3, 2011            15\n\n(b) the person does so with the intention of misleading a court or\njudicial tribunal in a judicial proceeding; and\n\n(c) the judicial proceeding is a federal judicial proceeding.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-36-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-36-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c5414b0437b09fb10a0edc47990c3812e2f9543f285a2abcb60b1ef430915258"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-2-sec-36",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36 Fabricating evidence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n(i) fabricates evidence; or\n\n(ii) makes use of fabricated evidence; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003\n\nAdministration of justice offences  Schedule 2\nAmendment of the Crimes Act 1914  Part 1\n\nLaw and Justice Legislation Amendment (Identity Crimes and Other Measures) Act 2011       No.\n3, 2011            15\n\n(b) the person does so with the intention of misleading a court or\njudicial tribunal in a judicial proceeding; and\n\n(c) the judicial proceeding is a federal judicial proceeding.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code."
    },
