      },
      "dc:source": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(b) the first person prevents the other person from attending as a\nwitness, or from producing anything in evidence, pursuant to\nthe subpoena or summons; and\n\n(c) the judicial proceeding is a federal judicial proceeding.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 1 year.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.",
      "skos:definition": "(b) the first person prevents the other person from attending as a\nwitness, or from producing anything in evidence, pursuant to\nthe subpoena or summons; and\n\n(c) the judicial proceeding is a federal judicial proceeding.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 1 year.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-2011-4-norm"
