      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person conspires with another person:\n\n(i) to charge any person falsely with an offence; or\n\n(ii) to cause any person to be falsely charged with an\noffence; and\n\n(b) the offence referred to in paragraph (a) is an offence against a\nlaw of:\n\n(i) the Commonwealth; or\n\n(ii) a Territory.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(1A) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(b) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person conspires with another person:\n\n(i) to charge any person falsely with an offence; or\n\n(ii) to cause any person to be falsely charged with an\noffence; and\n\n(b) the offence referred to in paragraph (a) is an offence against a\nlaw of:\n\n(i) the Commonwealth; or\n\n(ii) a Territory.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(1A) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(b) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-13-ss-1"
        },
