      },
      "dc:source": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person attempts to obstruct, to prevent, to pervert or to\ndefeat the course of justice in relation to a judicial power; and\n\n(b) the judicial power is the judicial power of the\nCommonwealth.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(b) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person attempts to obstruct, to prevent, to pervert or to\ndefeat the course of justice in relation to a judicial power; and\n\n(b) the judicial power is the judicial power of the\nCommonwealth.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(b) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-15-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-15-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "45006b563b2fa2182b7ea81cca2aac16faa404d7946d1c0f51f91fbff6cf069d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-2-sec-15",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15 Subsections 43(1) and (2)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person attempts to obstruct, to prevent, to pervert or to\ndefeat the course of justice in relation to a judicial power; and\n\n(b) the judicial power is the judicial power of the\nCommonwealth.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(b) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code."
    },
