        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1b504625a2ab0dec312cb57139ef2934add1a83ea7d20152ffc5104eb3e58dec",
      "skos:note": "Conveying a thing into a prison with the intention of facilitating escape is an offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-2-sec-2011-6-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2011(1) No. 3, 2011",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:\n\n(a) another person (the prisoner) is in criminal detention; and\n\n(b) the first person conveys a thing into a prison, lock-up or other\nplace of criminal detention; and\n\n(c) the first person does so with the intention of facilitating the\nescape of the prisoner from the prison, lock-up or other place;\nand\n\n(d) the detention is lawful federal criminal detention.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years."
    },
    {
