    {
      "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-47c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47C Permitting escape",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-2-sec-47c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person is:\n\n(i) an officer of a prison, lock-up or other place of criminal\ndetention; or\n\n(ii) a constable; or\n\n(iii) a Commonwealth officer; and\n\n(b) the first person is charged for the time being with the\ncriminal detention of another person (the prisoner); and\n\n(c) the first person intentionally or negligently permits the\nprisoner to escape from the detention; and\n\n(d) the detention is lawful federal criminal detention.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(d) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person is:\n\n(i) an officer of a prison, lock-up or other place of criminal\ndetention; or\n\n(ii) a constable; or\n\n(iii) a Commonwealth officer; and\n\n(b) the first person is charged for the time being with the\ncriminal detention of another person (the prisoner); and\n\n(c) the first person intentionally or negligently permits the\nprisoner to escape from the detention; and\n\n(d) the detention is lawful federal criminal detention.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(d) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-47c-ss-1"
        },
        {
