    {
      "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-49",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "49 Removing property under seizure",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-2-sec-49"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) property has been attached, or taken, under the process or\nauthority of a court; and\n\n(b) the court was:\n\n(i) a federal court; or\n\n(ii) exercising federal jurisdiction; or\n\n(iii) a court of a Territory; and\n\n(c) the person receives, removes, retains, conceals or disposes of\nthe property; and\n\n(d) the person does so with the intention of hindering or\ndefeating the attachment or process.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(b) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003\n\nSchedule 2  Administration of justice offences",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) property has been attached, or taken, under the process or\nauthority of a court; and\n\n(b) the court was:\n\n(i) a federal court; or\n\n(ii) exercising federal jurisdiction; or\n\n(iii) a court of a Territory; and\n\n(c) the person receives, removes, retains, conceals or disposes of\nthe property; and\n\n(d) the person does so with the intention of hindering or\ndefeating the attachment or process.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(b) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003\n\nSchedule 2  Administration of justice offences",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-49-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-49-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e1891380dbd6e62aeacbb4438105281822afc146612734f426c78e7033f9d289"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-2-sec-49",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "49 Removing property under seizure",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 29,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) property has been attached, or taken, under the process or\nauthority of a court; and\n\n(b) the court was:\n\n(i) a federal court; or\n\n(ii) exercising federal jurisdiction; or\n\n(iii) a court of a Territory; and\n\n(c) the person receives, removes, retains, conceals or disposes of\nthe property; and\n\n(d) the person does so with the intention of hindering or\ndefeating the attachment or process.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(b) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003\n\nSchedule 2  Administration of justice offences"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-49-ss-1",
