    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-24-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24 After section 56",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-2-sec-24-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n56A  Aiding persons to escape etc.\n\nDivision 5 of Part III of the Crimes Act 1914 has effect as if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003\n\nAdministration of justice offences  Schedule 2\nOther amendments  Part 2\n\nLaw and Justice Legislation Amendment (Identity Crimes and Other Measures) Act 2011       No.\n3, 2011            27\n\n(a) custody or detention in Australia under this Act were custody\nin respect of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth;\nand\n\n(b) arrest under section 56 of this Act were arrest in respect of an\noffence against a law of the Commonwealth.\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n56A  Aiding persons to escape etc.\n\nDivision 5 of Part III of the Crimes Act 1914 has effect as if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003\n\nAdministration of justice offences  Schedule 2\nOther amendments  Part 2\n\nLaw and Justice Legislation Amendment (Identity Crimes and Other Measures) Act 2011       No.\n3, 2011            27\n\n(a) custody or detention in Australia under this Act were custody\nin respect of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth;\nand\n\n(b) arrest under section 56 of this Act were arrest in respect of an\noffence against a law of the Commonwealth.\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-24-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-24-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f3b750753ec361f6db2a0fa67c5be02b6f0ea37720a56b71c78ffa296e6262bb",
      "skos:note": "Inserts definitions and amendments related to custody, detention, arrest, and war crimes tribunals."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-2-sec-24-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24 After section 56",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n56A  Aiding persons to escape etc.\n\nDivision 5 of Part III of the Crimes Act 1914 has effect as if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003\n\nAdministration of justice offences  Schedule 2\nOther amendments  Part 2\n\nLaw and Justice Legislation Amendment (Identity Crimes and Other Measures) Act 2011       No.\n3, 2011            27\n\n(a) custody or detention in Australia under this Act were custody\nin respect of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth;\nand\n\n(b) arrest under section 56 of this Act were arrest in respect of an\noffence against a law of the Commonwealth.\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995"
    },
