      "dc:source": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "31A  Aiding persons to escape etc.\n\nSections 46, 46A, 47A, 47C and 48 of the Crimes Act 1914 have\neffect as if:\n\n(a) arrest under section 31 of this Act were arrest in respect of an\noffence against a law of the Commonwealth; and\n\n(b) custody while in Australia in accordance with a direction\nunder paragraph 29(1)(d) of this Act were custody in respect\nof an offence against a law of the Commonwealth.\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979",
      "skos:definition": "31A  Aiding persons to escape etc.\n\nSections 46, 46A, 47A, 47C and 48 of the Crimes Act 1914 have\neffect as if:\n\n(a) arrest under section 31 of this Act were arrest in respect of an\noffence against a law of the Commonwealth; and\n\n(b) custody while in Australia in accordance with a direction\nunder paragraph 29(1)(d) of this Act were custody in respect\nof an offence against a law of the Commonwealth.\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-2011-9-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-2011-9-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "edb1153b3548cb65491ab6166900bedd9e28c7ac1bd5fd48bb88397d81692f4a",
      "skos:note": "Arrest under section 31 of the Act is considered an arrest in respect of a Commonwealth offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-2-sec-2011-9",
