      "cml:conclusionText": "Person need not accept function"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-3-sec-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 After subsection 31(1A)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-3-sec-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1B) The Director may, either generally or as otherwise provided by the\ninstrument of delegation, by writing signed by him or her, delegate\nto:\n\n(a) a person performing a similar role under a law of a State or\nTerritory; or\n\n(b) a member of the staff of a State or Territory authority (within\nthe meaning of subsection 15(3)) who is a legal practitioner;\nor\n\n(c) a person authorised by, or under, a law of a State or Territory\nto institute or conduct prosecutions for offences against the\nlaws of the State or Territory; or\n\n(d) a person included in a class of persons prescribed by the\nregulations for the purposes of this paragraph;\nall or any of the Director’s functions and powers under the\nfollowing provisions:\n\n(e) paragraphs 6(1)(a), (b), (c), (d) and (e);\n\n(f) paragraph 6(1)(n) (so far as it relates to the functions covered\nby paragraph (e) of this subsection);\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003\n\nSchedule 3  Director of Public Prosecutions Act 1983",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(1B) The Director may, either generally or as otherwise provided by the\ninstrument of delegation, by writing signed by him or her, delegate\nto:\n\n(a) a person performing a similar role under a law of a State or\nTerritory; or\n\n(b) a member of the staff of a State or Territory authority (within\nthe meaning of subsection 15(3)) who is a legal practitioner;\nor\n\n(c) a person authorised by, or under, a law of a State or Territory\nto institute or conduct prosecutions for offences against the\nlaws of the State or Territory; or\n\n(d) a person included in a class of persons prescribed by the\nregulations for the purposes of this paragraph;\nall or any of the Director’s functions and powers under the\nfollowing provisions:\n\n(e) paragraphs 6(1)(a), (b), (c), (d) and (e);\n\n(f) paragraph 6(1)(n) (so far as it relates to the functions covered\nby paragraph (e) of this subsection);\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003\n\nSchedule 3  Director of Public Prosecutions Act 1983",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-3-sec-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-3-sec-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-3-sec-4-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bbcbfb7d5d093dd2d971ea27604158dcac75a513d56b24fef5d863a88cbe2d70",
      "skos:note": "Director may delegate functions and powers to certain persons or authorities."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011#sch-3-sec-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 After subsection 31(1A)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1B) The Director may, either generally or as otherwise provided by the\ninstrument of delegation, by writing signed by him or her, delegate\nto:\n\n(a) a person performing a similar role under a law of a State or\nTerritory; or\n\n(b) a member of the staff of a State or Territory authority (within\nthe meaning of subsection 15(3)) who is a legal practitioner;\nor\n\n(c) a person authorised by, or under, a law of a State or Territory\nto institute or conduct prosecutions for offences against the\nlaws of the State or Territory; or\n\n(d) a person included in a class of persons prescribed by the\nregulations for the purposes of this paragraph;\nall or any of the Director’s functions and powers under the\nfollowing provisions:\n\n(e) paragraphs 6(1)(a), (b), (c), (d) and (e);\n\n(f) paragraph 6(1)(n) (so far as it relates to the functions covered\nby paragraph (e) of this subsection);\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003\n\nSchedule 3  Director of Public Prosecutions Act 1983"
    },
